From c33ef2de09cbc5d3700a816b0e341160cf5cba4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Hope <15705900+gabehope@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:27:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] WebGPU dispatches share one command encoder and submit per
 task

Every dispatch created a command encoder, ~2 bind groups, a uniform
write and a queue submit: about 715 submits for one brush move over
heatmaptest's brushed distributions. Dispatches are now encoded into a
batch submitted at the end of the task that opened it, after 256
dispatches, or before anything that must see their results: a read,
gpuBuffer(), or a wait. A batch's uniforms sit at distinct offsets of the
shared uniform buffer, written once before its submit, and each
pipeline's uniform bind group is cached while that buffer stays. Buffers
released while a batch is open are held until it is submitted, so an
upload into a reused buffer cannot land before commands that still read
it, and nothing it references is destroyed early. While tracing, a
dispatch is still submitted on its own (its timestamps resolve per
dispatch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/backend/webgpu.ts | 210 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/frontend/array.ts |   3 +
 2 files changed, 192 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

